    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d543">

                <pb facs="0599" n="591" xml:id="pg591"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.4016/2125: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-07-21T16:00:00-04:00">July 21, 1939—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>308. Your despatch 1043, June 23, 1939. Please address a note to Minister of
                    Foreign Affairs and referring to report published in the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Deutsche Allgemeine Zeitung</hi> concerning proposed regulations imposing
                    restrictions upon Jews visiting health and bathing resorts and add: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>I have been instructed by my Government to call attention to its several
                            representations, and particularly to those contained in the Embassy’s
                            notes of May 9<anchor n="59" xml:id="d543-f1"/> and December 14,
                                1938<anchor n="59a" xml:id="d543-f2"/> and January 6, 1939.<anchor
                                n="60" xml:id="d543-f3"/> against the imposition in Germany of
                            discriminations upon American citizens based on race or creed, and to
                            state that the Government of the United States assumes that the
                            discriminatory treatment indicated in the report will not be applied to
                            American nationals of the Jewish race.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
